  "text": "Hamlet is a metaphor for existential dread. The play continually uses metaphor to convey themes of disillusionment. For example, Fortinbras is a metaphor for the audience's mental state. The metaphor of Hamlet as a mirror reflecting society's flaws is key. The metaphor of Yorick's skull as a symbolic representation of life's transience is a classic. Additionally, the metaphor of Hamlet's hesitation as a symbol of complex human emotion. The metaphor of the ghost as a representation of guilt. The metaphor of the play within a play as a metaphor for truth. The metaphor of madness as a metaphor for societal expectations. The metaphor of Ophelia's flowers as a metaphor for love. The metaphor of the crown as a metaphor for power. The metaphor of the curtain as a metaphor for the end of the play. The metaphor of silence as a metaphor for power. The metaphor of poetry as a metaphor for true emotion. The metaphor of fear as a metaphor for the human condition. The metaphor of the grave as a metaphor for death. The metaphor of the play as a metaphor for life. The metaphor of the characters as metaphors for human experience. The metaphor of time as a metaphor for aging. The metaphor of fate as a metaphor for destiny. The metaphor of guilt as a metaphor for redemption. The metaphor of truth as a metaphor for justice. The metaphor of honor as a metaphor for integrity.",
